32d8154c01c69c7dbba3de00c428a65b7fd756c9ec18fce","event_uuid":"e90393f9-ae28-49c5-8eeb-899c320f845c","position":{"commit_sha":"86d3e2110fd28db4b3a33088675b99608a536682","position":"1788283591478046368-e90393f9-ae28-49c5-8eeb-899c320f845c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"72fa831f544a33edceaed39034a6c8e0825678f8d61870012c76d4c9d52c5500","event_uuid":"1afb159b-5f00-48f0-b64b-ea94c8c4c2d4","position":{"commit_sha":"86d3e2110fd28db4b3a33088675b99608a536682","position":"1788283591496252290-1afb159b-5f00-48f0-b64b-ea94c8c4c2d4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review BLOCK on 2026-08-31 before claim/code edits. First plan was blocked because it only batched TICKET_DIGEST+DONE_ENRICH and did not satisfy AC1's one-commit quartet. Revised plan proposed an internal leased reservation so ENQUEUE/CLAIM/TICKET_DIGEST/DONE could commit together, but review still BLOCKED: replacing the pre-LLM git-visible CLAIM_ENRICH with non-git state would not arbitrate duplicate spend across clones, and _live_drainer_ids/_MAX_CONCURRENT_DRAINERS currently census committed CLAIM_ENRICH events. This is a design conflict between AC1's single commit and the existing cross-clone claim/audit contract. Per constraints, I did not claim, edit source, or bypass gates.","timestamp":1788239126295670001}],"created_at":1788046542480098623,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"36bcc7cb-9ee5-42d3-9dc4-f8b9e9f98236","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"21d1-3715-30bd-40d7"},{"link_uuid":"1ab9e230-cc14-41d9-8b73-2c7674adaf50","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe `tickets` pack grows because enrichment writeback emits separate git commits that each re-emit the root tree. S1 reclaims historical churn; W1 reduces new post-enrich finalize churn at the source.\n\n## Scope\n\nBatch only the post-enrich finalize events for one successful enrichment item: `TICKET_DIGEST` + `DONE_ENRICH` collapse from two commits to one commit/root-tree re-emission. `CLAIM_ENRICH` remains its own committed and auto-pushed event, visible before the LLM/enrich call, because `_live_drainer_ids`, `_MAX_CONCURRENT_DRAINERS`, and `queue.claim()` arbitrate cross-clone drainers by reading committed post-enqueue `CLAIM_ENRICH` events. `ENQUEUE_ENRICH` remains unchanged as an earlier lifecycle event.\n\nPreserve observable ticket state, event semantics, per-event signing/verifiability, and optimistic-concurrency guarantees. Batch the git commit only; each event remains its own event file with its own authorship material.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nHistory reclaim (S1); event schema changes; queue claim arbitration changes; drainer concurrency-cap changes; enqueue timing changes; folding `CLAIM_ENRICH` into a batch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The post-enrich finalize events (`TICKET_DIGEST` + `DONE_ENRICH`) for a single successful enrichment item collapse into ONE commit/root-tree re-emission on a fixture; `CLAIM_ENRICH` remains a separate committed event for cross-clone drainer arbitration.\n- [ ] Observable reduced ticket state is unchanged vs the pre-batch behavior (public-reader/reducer fixture passes).\n- [ ] Each batched event retains its individual signature and passes `rebar verify-authorship`.\n- [ ] Optimistic-concurrency / audit guarantees are preserved: existing drainer arbitration and concurrency tests pass, and `CLAIM_ENRICH` stays visible before enrichment.\n- [ ] Commits-per-enrich-burst and per-burst root-tree re-emissions drop from CLAIM + DIGEST + DONE (3 commits) to CLAIM + batched-finalize (2 commits); `ENQUEUE_ENRICH` remains a separate earlier lifecycle event.\n\n## Portability\n\nPure library/store change; no dependence on any single CI provider.\n\n## Implementation plan (2026-09-01, narrowed by operator decision)\n\n### Worked example\n\nFor an already-soaked queued ticket, drain currently emits committed `CLAIM_ENRICH`, then after the LLM returns emits committed `TICKET_DIGEST`, then committed `DONE_ENRICH`. W1 keeps CLAIM exactly as-is. The normal-path finalize lane composes `TICKET_DIGEST {schema, digest, content_hash, model, digest_hash_version}` and `DONE_ENRICH {ticket_id}` as separate signed events but flushes them through one batch commit.\n\nPartial-failure example: if digest event composition/signing is refused and `digest_sidecar.emit()` returns `False`, `queue.mark_done()` is still called exactly as current code does. The batch buffer contains whatever the existing helpers successfully composed (DONE only in that example) and flushes that. If the batch commit itself fails after events were composed, the helper logs and falls back to the existing sequential direct calls in order (`digest_sidecar.emit()` then `queue.mark_done()` outside the sink). This preserves the previous best-effort failure posture; the optimization is the normal successful path, not a new durability contract under store faults.\n\n### Mechanism\n\n1. In `rebar.llm.enrich_drain._finalize_claims`, replace the success path's two independent normal writes with an enrichment-local helper that opens `_commands._seam.batch_sink`, calls `digest_sidecar.emit(...)` and `queue.mark_done(...)` in the same order and with the same ignored return-value contract as today, then flushes the buffered events with `_store.event_append.batch_write_and_push()`.\n2. Preserve helper best-effort semantics: composition/signing failures are swallowed by existing helpers; the following helper call still runs; an empty buffer returns without a commit. Batch commit failures degrade to the old sequential direct write path after rollback, with a warning.\n3. Do not change `queue.enqueue`, `queue.claim`, `queue.mark_done`, `digest_sidecar.emit`, event schema, `_live_drainer_ids`, `_MAX_CONCURRENT_DRAINERS`, or queue reducers. The public event stream after successful finalize still contains the same `TICKET_DIGEST` and `DONE_ENRICH` events in order; only the wrapping git commit count changes.\n4. Leave permanent-rejection tombstones and stale-writeback re-enqueue behavior unchanged. CLAIM remains outside the batch by design and visible before enrichment.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\nA. Batch only the post-enrich finalize pair: chosen by the operator on 2026-09-01. B. Batch CLAIM with finalize using local reservations: rejected because committed CLAIM events are the cross-clone coordination contract. C. Hold the drain advisory lock across the LLM: rejected because existing concurrency work requires enrichment outside the advisory lock. D. Make the finalize pair strictly atomic with no fallback: rejected because W1 should not change best-effort store-fault behavior.\n\n### Test plan / RED-first oracle\n\n- Add a fixture test in `tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py`: enqueue a ticket, record tracker commit count, run one drain, and assert exactly two new commits: one containing `CLAIM_ENRICH`, and one containing both `TICKET_DIGEST` and `DONE_ENRICH`.\n- Assert public postconditions in that fixture: digest present/fresh, queue `done == True`, `pending == False`, and sidecar events do not alter schema-visible ticket state.\n- Run fixture-appropriate `rebar verify-authorship` after batched finalize to prove each batched event retains individual signing/verifiability.\n- Run existing arbitration/concurrency tests, especially `test_concurrent_drains_make_zero_duplicate_llm_calls`, to prove `CLAIM_ENRICH` visibility is unchanged.\n- Add a targeted partial-failure unit test by monkeypatching the batch flush to raise after buffered composition, asserting the old direct helper calls are invoked in order as fallback.\n- Preflight with targeted pytest first, then `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the project test gate before push.\n\n### Surface-parity census\n\nCLI command: in scope through `rebar enrich --drain`/`cmd_enrich` because it routes to `enrich_drain.drain`. MCP/API: no separate schema change; enrichment callers share the same library drain core, accepted residual gap unless a direct MCP enrich surface appears. Library facade: in scope through direct `enrich_drain.drain`, `queue`, and `digest_sidecar` fixture tests. Automated callers: in scope because `_store.event_append.write_and_push -> _maybe_enrich_drain -> maybe_drain -> drain` remains the automated path, with CLAIM still committed before enrichment. Read/dual direction: in scope through `latest_ticket_digest`, `freshness`, `queue.reduce_ticket`, and `pending_enrichment`; reducer-visible ticket state stays unchanged.\n\n### Acceptance mapping\n\nAC1/AC5: commit-count/root-tree tests showing CLAIM remains separate while finalize pair is one commit. AC2: public reducer/reader postconditions. AC3: authorship verification on the fixture. AC4: unchanged public queue contracts plus existing drain concurrency tests and fallback-order coverage.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py","reason":"Batch the post-enrich TICKET_DIGEST + DONE_ENRICH finalize writes while leaving CLAIM_ENRICH visible before enrichment."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py","reason":"RED-first fixture coverage for commit-count/root-tree reduction, public state invariants, authorship verification, and unchanged drainer arbitration."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"],["relates_to","21d1-3715-30bd-40d7"],["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"e90393f9-ae28-49c5-8eeb-899c320f845c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6816-69bf-460d-4db1","ticket_type":"task","title":"W1: batch enrichment quartet + digest into one write lane (cut ~14K commits/day at source)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["36bcc7cb-9ee5-42d3-9dc4-f8b9e9f98236","d5b30619-09be-4768-9072-7a66ec4e3cd1","c28b021e-ca10-4156-801f-d3050cf2b01f","c6b4294f-0f11-42fb-a289-8f636b503d17","79cd921d-a8a7-483d-829c-0a4d8fa37bf4","1be3d5b5-9998-4f2f-80c2-f7a5e2f51ec5","e8df5982-99c9-4527-b4d5-124e37f9cbc0","3b42b62f-4573-4be4-a872-3cb2fcf4d919","700e0c1c-4164-4a74-8f34-285a65147601","4c24b8ba-a71b-4230-9b3f-0612e4037b4d","1ab9e230-cc14-41d9-8b73-2c7674adaf50","e90393f9-ae28-49c5-8eeb-899c320f845c","1afb159b-5f00-48f0-b64b-ea94c8c4c2d4"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788283591496252291,"uuid":"727002a8-9a27-4514-94d4-274051427844"}